      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You should frame their argument as a dangerous form of short-sightedness that prioritizes the comfort of the current wealthy over the survival of the entire species. Their focus on \"not fully hit yet\" ignores the accelerating reality of climate tipping points where inaction guarantees catastrophic collapse regardless of future economic conditions. By labeling their stance as unethical, you can argue that they are actually being unethical to themselves by refusing to take the only viable path to prevent mass extinction. Ultimately, their concern is a rational fear of immediate pain, but it is a fear that will be proven wrong by the inevitable and far worse consequences of climate failure.",
